WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
- We are back

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.790
and 40 years ago, y'all,

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:05.490
the mother-daughter duo Naomi and Wynonna

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:08.580
broke ground in the country
music scene as The Judds.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.060
They earned Grammys,
CMA Awards, ACM Awards,

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.430
and we just love them so much.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.220
They were all set to do
a reunion tour in 2022

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.160
when, tragically, Naomi Judd passed away.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.020
To celebrate her momma's legacy,

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.330
and to raise awareness
about mental illness,

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.640
Wynonna Judd has released a new album

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.470
called "A Tribute to The Judds."

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.840
The artists who've contributed
are some of the best,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.940
Dolly Parton, Lainey Wilson, Jelly Roll,

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.230
and our next guest.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:37.560
Performing The Judd's classic,
"Cry Myself to Sleep,"

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.790
ooh, you ain't ready for this,

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.367
give it up for Wynonna
Judd and Trisha Yearwood!

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:45.660
(audience applauding)
(audience cheering)

